Subject: CVE-2026-102554 — bump bundled Guava to 33.7.2-jre

Gradle 9.8.2 pins Guava 33.4.6-jre in distribution.versions.toml. Maven Central
ships 33.7.2-jre with the fix for unbounded resource consumption in certain
cache paths.

Tracker: https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-102554
CVE: CVE-2026-102554
Origin: DHI-internal (bundled Gradle dependency bump)
Base-Tree: git https://github.com/gradle/gradle.git 8de7bcf76e785507ad92f0741ab9235a430c95e6
Regenerate: `sed -i 's/guava = "33.4.6-jre"/guava = "33.7.2-jre"/' gradle/dependency-management/distribution.versions.toml`
Forwarded: not-needed (no upstream Gradle commit yet)
Drop-When: dependency com.google.guava:guava >= 33.7.2-jre

diff --git a/gradle/dependency-management/distribution.versions.toml b/gradle/dependency-management/distribution.versions.toml
index 683df05b..a144e869 100644
--- a/gradle/dependency-management/distribution.versions.toml
+++ b/gradle/dependency-management/distribution.versions.toml
@@ -16,7 +16,7 @@ googleHttpClient = "1.42.2!!" # Covers googleHttpClient, googleHttpClientGson, g
 googleOauthClient = "1.34.1!!" # our Google API Client version requires 1.34.1
 gradleFileEvents = "0.2.8!!"
 gson = "2.13.1!!"
-guava = "33.4.6-jre"
+guava = "33.7.2-jre"
 httpcore = "4.4.16!!"
 inject = "1!!"
 ivy = "2.5.3!!"
